==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|sensuall}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sent-|id=perceive}}
From {{uder|en|la-lat|sensualis||endowed with feeling, sensual}}, from {{der|en|la|sensus||feeling, sense}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛnsjuːəl/|/ˈsɛnʃuːəl/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sensual.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛn.ʃu.əl/|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Inducing [[pleasurable]] or [[erotic]] sensations.
#: {{syn|en|sexy|voluptuous}}
#: {{ux|en|That massage was a very '''sensual''' experience!}}
# Of or pertaining to the physical [[senses]]; [[sensory]].
#: {{ux|en|Plato believed that this '''sensual''' world in which we live is inferior to the heavenly realm.}}
# Provoking or [[exciting]] a strong [[response]] in the [[sense]]s.

